1
00:00:00,389 --> 00:00:02,908
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:02,948 --> 00:00:07,400
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:08,265 --> 00:00:13,511
We're continuing with the leftovers from the section of Ribat(رباط).

4
00:00:15,384 --> 00:00:21,166
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) said: Allah has instructed us to become Muslim and we did.

5
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,253
So we are the Muslims.

6
00:00:23,991 --> 00:00:29,940
He then ordered us to make Hijrah(هجرة), so we did, the people of Makkah, and we are the Muhajireen(مهاجرين).

7
00:00:30,765 --> 00:00:33,119
He then told us to fight Jihad(جهاد) and you did.

8
00:00:33,555 --> 00:00:36,291
So you the people of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام), are the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

9
00:00:37,529 --> 00:00:42,127
Now here, it doesn't necessarily mean that people who are from Ash-Sham(ألشَّام),

10
00:00:42,182 --> 00:00:45,916
he is talking about the people who are based in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)

11
00:00:45,996 --> 00:00:50,140
the Sahabah(صحابه), who went to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) and settled there, for Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

12
00:00:50,788 --> 00:00:56,000
 Spend money on yourself and your family, and the needy around you!

13
00:00:56,420 --> 00:01:02,559
Since if you go out with a single Dirham(درهم) and bought some meat with it.

14
00:01:03,305 --> 00:01:09,396
And you ate it, you and your family would be rewarded as spending 700 Dirham(درهم)s.

15
00:01:11,526 --> 00:01:16,839
The interesting thing here in this statement of Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه

16
00:01:17,672 --> 00:01:22,598
is that, he even considers the money that you would spend on your family to be multiplied by 700.

17
00:01:24,225 --> 00:01:28,988
What Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) is saying that as a Murabat(مرابط), any money that you spend,

18
00:01:29,537 --> 00:01:33,749
even if it's for your food and the food of your family is multiplied by 700.

19
00:01:33,872 --> 00:01:36,808
Because the purpose of you being there is Ribat(رباط) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

20
00:01:37,157 --> 00:01:40,301
So anything that you spend as long as it's spent in a Halal(حلال) way,

21
00:01:40,689 --> 00:01:44,229
and without Asraaf(أسراف) extravagance is multiplied by 700.

22
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:51,780
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says: The spending in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) is multiplied if it is during the era of Uthman(عثمان),

23
00:01:52,169 --> 00:01:54,087
because all of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) was the land of Ribat(رباط),

24
00:01:54,227 --> 00:01:57,544
it was expected that the enemy could descend on any part of it.

25
00:01:58,155 --> 00:02:05,628
But now that applies only to the frontiers of it, which are exposed to the attacks by the enemy.

26
00:02:07,209 --> 00:02:13,831
The frontiers would be the northern parts of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) and also the coastal line,

27
00:02:14,299 --> 00:02:18,345
because the coastline of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) remained as the land of Ribat(رباط).

28
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:21,410
The Messenger of Allah said:

29
00:02:22,085 --> 00:02:27,130
There will be people from my nation who will protect the borders, they will fulfill their duty.

30
00:02:27,704 --> 00:02:29,788
But they will not be given what is due to them.

31
00:02:30,345 --> 00:02:32,617
They are from me, and I am from them.

32
00:02:34,171 --> 00:02:36,353
And this is in Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن ألمبارك) and it is Hasan(حسن).

33
00:02:36,830 --> 00:02:39,371
Rasool Allah ﷺ was talking about the obscure soldier,

34
00:02:40,363 --> 00:02:43,779
who's manning a post he's guarding Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عزَّوَجل).

35
00:02:44,466 --> 00:02:46,473
He's very simple, nobody really knows about him,

36
00:02:48,306 --> 00:02:51,346
but Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that these are the ones, who are guarding the Ummah(امة),

37
00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:54,687
and they are from me, and I am from them.

38
00:02:58,061 --> 00:03:01,167
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

39
00:03:02,395 --> 00:03:09,275
Among, the best livelihoods of people is that of a man holding the rein of his horse in the path of Allah,

40
00:03:09,854 --> 00:03:14,099
flying on its back, whenever he hears a call.

41
00:03:14,417 --> 00:03:15,026
The Hadith(حديث) says:

42
00:03:15,074 --> 00:03:16,056
يطيرو على متن

43
00:03:17,161 --> 00:03:18,857
Now, horses don't fly,

44
00:03:19,852 --> 00:03:23,017
but Rasool Allah ﷺ used the word Yateer Alaa Mat'ne(يطيرعلى متن)

45
00:03:23,523 --> 00:03:29,754
on his back to mean that this man, whenever he hears the call of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

46
00:03:30,206 --> 00:03:31,889
he swiftly responds to it.

47
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:38,401
It is as if he is flying to go and fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), and what is he flying for...?

48
00:03:38,825 --> 00:03:41,148
He flies in search of killing or being killed.

49
00:03:42,333 --> 00:03:43,558
ليقتل أو يقتل

50
00:03:44,984 --> 00:03:49,702
And the man on top of a mountain peak or on the bottom of a deep valley,

51
00:03:50,365 --> 00:03:55,317
establishing prayers paying his Zaka'at(زكوة) and worshiping his Lord, until death visits him.

52
00:03:55,825 --> 00:03:57,881
People see nothing from him, but good.

53
00:03:58,913 --> 00:04:00,357
And this is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح ألمسلم).

54
00:04:01,354 --> 00:04:06,784
So again, this is in the time of fittan(فتن), the best way to live is either as a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد)

55
00:04:07,369 --> 00:04:12,599
or as a person who is seeking Halal(حلال) Rizq(رزق) away from people away from the fittan(فتن),

56
00:04:13,006 --> 00:04:15,885
away from the temptations.

57
00:04:16,238 --> 00:04:21,369
Two men came to the companion, Abdullah Bin Al-Haris Bin Juzae Az-Zabedi(عبدالله بن ألحارث بن جزء ألزبيدي).

58
00:04:22,755 --> 00:04:25,140
 He said welcome, and he handed them a pillow.

59
00:04:25,717 --> 00:04:29,450
So these two men are At-Taba'een(ألتابعين), they visited a Sahabi(صحابي).

60
00:04:31,048 --> 00:04:32,496
But even though he was a Sahabi(صحابي).

61
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:35,589
He was the one, who was serving them,

62
00:04:35,629 --> 00:04:39,836
you know, they didn't have the tradition of going in and kissing the knees or the hands.

63
00:04:40,861 --> 00:04:43,469
These are At-Taba'een(ألتابعين), who came in to somebody who was senior.

64
00:04:43,988 --> 00:04:46,524
This is a Sahabi(صحابي) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, he is old in age.

65
00:04:47,170 --> 00:04:50,354
Nevertheless, when they came in he was giving them pillows to sit on.

66
00:04:51,501 --> 00:04:56,558
They said: We did not come for this but we came for you to tell us something that would benefit us, a hadith(حديث).

67
00:04:57,522 --> 00:04:58,028
He said:

68
00:04:58,377 --> 00:05:02,394
Whoever does not treat his guests with generosity does not belong to Muhammad(محمد) and Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

69
00:05:02,641 --> 00:05:03,874
it's is not part of the Hadith(حديث).

70
00:05:04,377 --> 00:05:07,171
He's just telling them that I need to be generous to you.

71
00:05:07,530 --> 00:05:11,195
Because whoever is not generous doesn't belong to Muhammadﷺ and Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

72
00:05:11,715 --> 00:05:15,563
And when it comes to generosity we consider Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), to be the father of generosity.

73
00:05:16,512 --> 00:05:27,234
Ibrahim عليه السّلام, he received three angels, and he slaughtered for them, a calf, a whole calf.

74
00:05:28,792 --> 00:05:31,784
And he could have presented them with something else

75
00:05:31,885 --> 00:05:34,691
but out of his generosity, he slaughtered for them Ijl(عجل),

76
00:05:34,731 --> 00:05:40,478
and this Ijl(عجل) might have meant a lot for the family of Ibrahim عليه السّلام, but he slaughtered it for them.

77
00:05:41,105 --> 00:05:46,577
And the Ayah(آية) describes it, as in one Ayah(آية), Ijl Sameen(عجل سمين).

78
00:05:47,409 --> 00:05:52,894
He is fat, and in the other Ayah(آية) Ijl Haneez(عجل حنيذ), it is roasted.

79
00:05:53,585 --> 00:05:59,988
So we know from these two Ayaat(آيات) that it was Ijl(عجل) calf, and it was big, fat, and it was roasted.

80
00:06:00,604 --> 00:06:04,090
So it was barbecued meat that he served to the angels.

81
00:06:06,063 --> 00:06:09,877
But the problem was they didn't even eat it, because they were Malaikah(ملائكة).

82
00:06:10,454 --> 00:06:13,045
Blessed is he, so this is the Hadith(حديث) that is telling them.

83
00:06:13,802 --> 00:06:18,966
Blessed is he, who spends his night holding the rain of his horse in the path of Allah.

84
00:06:19,716 --> 00:06:22,552
Having a piece of dry bread and water as his breakfast,

85
00:06:23,410 --> 00:06:28,992
and woe to those who are feeding like cows, saying servant, take this and servant bring that,

86
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:32,385
all of that and they don't even remember Allah.

87
00:06:33,566 --> 00:06:37,183
So they just eat and eat and eat without even saying Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله), when they finish

88
00:06:37,223 --> 00:06:38,273
or Bismillah(بسم الله) when they start.

89
00:06:38,652 --> 00:06:41,810
What about the period of being stationed, how long should it be?

90
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:47,320
Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) was asked, is there any period for being stationed he said 40 days.

91
00:06:47,821 --> 00:06:50,466
So, you should have your 40 days Khurooj(خروج) in Ribat(رباط).

92
00:06:52,746 --> 00:06:53,645
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) said:

93
00:06:54,341 --> 00:06:57,136
For me to be stationed for one night, next to the sea,

94
00:06:57,853 --> 00:07:01,724
and protecting the Muslims behind me is better than spending the night of Al-Qadr(ألقدر)

95
00:07:02,763 --> 00:07:05,840
in the Masjid(مسجد) of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), or the Masjid(مسجد) of the Messenger of Allah.

96
00:07:06,799 --> 00:07:09,591
And spending three days of Ribat(رباط) is equal to a whole year.

97
00:07:10,139 --> 00:07:12,740
And the most complete period of Ribat(رباط) is 40 days.

98
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:14,864
This is by Abdur Razzaq(عبدالرزاق).

99
00:07:16,509 --> 00:07:19,440
A man from Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

100
00:07:19,735 --> 00:07:21,037
So Umar(عُمَر) ask him where were you.?

101
00:07:21,802 --> 00:07:22,930
He said I was in Ribat(رباط).

102
00:07:23,541 --> 00:07:24,593
Umar(عُمَر) said: For how long?

103
00:07:24,633 --> 00:07:25,654
He said: 30 days.

104
00:07:26,022 --> 00:07:28,585
Umar(عُمَر) said: You should have completed it 40.

105
00:07:29,290 --> 00:07:30,789
Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه said:

106
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:35,973
If you spent three days in Ribat(رباط), then let the worshippers, worship as they wish.

107
00:07:36,987 --> 00:07:39,355
Ibn-e-Abi Shaibah(إبن أبي شعيبة), and it is authentic.

108
00:07:40,869 --> 00:07:49,196
What he means by that is, no one can compete with the Ajr(أجْر) of three days Ribat(رباط) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah عزَّوَجل.

109
00:07:50,953 --> 00:07:51,970
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

110
00:07:52,851 --> 00:07:59,828
The command in Ar-Ribat(ألرباط) is for a person to station himself to a vulnerable land, where the enemy is expected to attack.

111
00:08:00,686 --> 00:08:03,338
The word Ribat(رباط) comes from Rabata(ربطة), which is to tie.

112
00:08:04,445 --> 00:08:08,559
The Murabit(مرابط) does that with the intention of fighting the enemy or guarding the land,

113
00:08:08,999 --> 00:08:11,849
or even to increase the number of Muslims in that land,

114
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:18,605
the more dangerous the land is, the more rewarding it becomes, whether it is a seaport, or otherwise.

115
00:08:18,985 --> 00:08:22,444
Imam Malik(إمام مالك), does not consider Ribat(رباط) in Jeddah(جدَّة), to be Ribat(رباط),

116
00:08:23,028 --> 00:08:25,272
because the enemy only attacked it once.

117
00:08:26,347 --> 00:08:32,140
Imam Malik(إمام مالك) was also asked his opinion on the ones who live in the land of Ribat(رباط) with their families.

118
00:08:32,642 --> 00:08:33,169
He said:

119
00:08:33,544 --> 00:08:35,546
They are not considered Murabiteen(مرابطين),

120
00:08:36,686 --> 00:08:41,907
because the Murabit(مرابط) is the one, who leaves from his home with the intention of Ribat(رباط) in a land of danger.

121
00:08:42,491 --> 00:08:45,790
It appears to me that the one, who is living in an area of Ribat(رباط),

122
00:08:46,029 --> 00:08:50,212
and the only intention, he has is staying there is the Jihad(جهاد) or guarding the land,

123
00:08:50,638 --> 00:08:53,839
and this person has the ability to move to another place without difficulty.

124
00:08:54,318 --> 00:08:59,689
My opinion is that such a person is Murabit(مرابط) and would be rewarded accordingly,

125
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:02,269
even if he is accompanied by his family.

126
00:09:02,896 --> 00:09:07,126
The Sahabah(صحابه) and At-Tabieen(تابعين) used to live in the land of Ribat(رباط) with their families,

127
00:09:07,483 --> 00:09:09,450
with the intention of Ribat(رباط).

128
00:09:10,094 --> 00:09:15,231
Maybe what Imam Malik(إمام مالك) meant was, those who were born in the land of Ribat(رباط), and brought up there,

129
00:09:15,787 --> 00:09:18,189
and they lived there because it was their homeland,

130
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:22,803
and the place where their families lived, and they are not there for the purpose of Ribat(رباط).

131
00:09:23,462 --> 00:09:26,422
This is also the opinion of Ibn Atiyyah(إبن عطية), He states that

132
00:09:26,888 --> 00:09:29,808
 the ones, who live in the land of Ribat(رباط) because it is their home,

133
00:09:30,089 --> 00:09:34,789
and the place of their work are considered protectors of the land, but not Murabiteen(مرابطين).

134
00:09:35,237 --> 00:09:36,052
So to make it simple.

135
00:09:37,192 --> 00:09:40,915
Niyyah(نية) is the key issue here.

136
00:09:41,328 --> 00:09:46,323
If a person is living in that place with the intention of Ribat(رباط) and Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah then he Is Murabit(مرابط).

137
00:09:46,955 --> 00:09:51,457
If the intention is because of money, because of work, because this is my homeland, because I love it.

138
00:09:52,146 --> 00:09:54,751
I'm attached to the land, it's a different intention.

139
00:09:56,014 --> 00:10:00,618
So the ones, who lives in the land of Ribat(رباط) for a purpose that does not exist in other places,

140
00:10:00,964 --> 00:10:06,010
or because his family insists on living there, or for the purpose of work is not a Murabit(مرابط).

141
00:10:06,657 --> 00:10:10,753
Also, If a person is in the place of Ribat(رباط) and the danger of the enemy ceases to exist.

142
00:10:11,268 --> 00:10:14,401
And nevertheless, this person continues to live in that place,

143
00:10:14,847 --> 00:10:18,887
that is an indication that the purpose of such a person is not Jihad(جهاد)

144
00:10:18,918 --> 00:10:21,831
and thus the person does not qualify as a Murabit(مرابط).

145
00:10:22,804 --> 00:10:26,353
Now if there is a person living in the land of Ribat(رباط) and his intention is that

146
00:10:26,424 --> 00:10:28,726
whenever the enemy attacks, he would run away,

147
00:10:29,511 --> 00:10:31,988
then such a person is living in a state of sin,

148
00:10:32,644 --> 00:10:36,389
because the moment the enemy attacks, it becomes a major sin to runaway.

149
00:10:36,950 --> 00:10:39,910
So such a person is better off moving from the land of Ribat(رباط),

150
00:10:40,174 --> 00:10:43,684
because he is accumulating sin, all the time, with such an intention.

151
00:10:45,138 --> 00:10:52,339
So, In the area is that one could consider now as land of Ribat(رباط)

152
00:10:53,400 --> 00:11:01,527
like Afghanistan, Iraq, Kashmir, Chechnya, because whenever there's lull in fighting,

153
00:11:02,427 --> 00:11:07,894
it doesn't mean that the fighting has seized, you know, the fight still carries on, because these are invaded lands

154
00:11:08,803 --> 00:11:09,575
or Falastine(فلسطين).

155
00:11:10,787 --> 00:11:17,195
If a person is living there, and their intention is that when an attack would come I would leave,

156
00:11:19,343 --> 00:11:21,333
then such a person is accumulating sin

157
00:11:21,373 --> 00:11:26,626
and this tells us something that living in the land of Ribat(رباط) could either be a blessing or it could be a curse.

158
00:11:27,107 --> 00:11:28,889
You know you can't get out of it even.

159
00:11:29,957 --> 00:11:37,067
You either may come out of Hasanat(حسانات), or you lose a lot of Hasanat(حسانات) by the mere existence in that place.

160
00:11:39,183 --> 00:11:41,197
Virtues of guarding in the path of Allah.

161
00:11:43,001 --> 00:11:45,403
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrated the Prophet said:

162
00:11:46,168 --> 00:11:51,673
Let the slave of Dinar(دينار) and Dirham(درهم) of quantify and Qameesa(قميصه) perish, as he is pleased.

163
00:11:53,094 --> 00:11:54,913
If these things are given to him.

164
00:11:55,793 --> 00:11:57,311
And if not, he is displeased.

165
00:11:57,658 --> 00:12:05,310
تعس عبد الدينار تعس عبد الدرهم تعس عبد القطيفة تعس عبد الخميصة،

166
00:12:05,787 --> 00:12:07,930
Rasool Allah ﷺ is making Dua(دُعَا) on these people.

167
00:12:08,717 --> 00:12:10,151
He is saying: May they perish.

168
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:12,929
إذا عطي رضي

169
00:12:13,147 --> 00:12:16,723
If they are given, they are pleased if they are not, they're displeased.

170
00:12:17,108 --> 00:12:23,788
So the matter that controls their heart feelings is wealth, whether it goes up or down.

171
00:12:24,282 --> 00:12:25,903
That's the whole purpose of life.

172
00:12:27,197 --> 00:12:30,820
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying Taisa(تعس), Taisa(تعس) is Dua(دُعَا) against them.

173
00:12:31,931 --> 00:12:33,967
May they perish and then Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

174
00:12:34,189 --> 00:12:35,286
تعس وانتكس

175
00:12:36,072 --> 00:12:40,614
 And Takas(تكس) means: If you fall down, and then you try to stand up again you fall down again.

176
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:47,935
Meaning, let this person fall down and then fall down again and not be able to stand up.

177
00:12:48,382 --> 00:12:49,739
وإذا شيكَ فلا انتقشَ

178
00:12:50,553 --> 00:12:56,377
And if they are hit with a thorn, let him not find anyone to take it out of him.

179
00:12:57,918 --> 00:13:01,966
Because with thorns, you have a certain clip that pulls it out.

180
00:13:03,432 --> 00:13:05,513
And you might need the help of somebody to do that for you.

181
00:13:05,553 --> 00:13:09,523
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying may these people not have anybody to help them.

182
00:13:10,004 --> 00:13:12,068
Why? Because their intentions are purely for Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

183
00:13:12,650 --> 00:13:13,886
This is figurative speech here,

184
00:13:13,966 --> 00:13:24,828
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that a person whose sole intention is Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), and they are servants and slaves of wealth.

185
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:27,677
May these people not succeed in what they want

186
00:13:30,104 --> 00:13:35,561
and whenever they fall down into a problem or catastrophe, financial problem or whatever it is,

187
00:13:35,890 --> 00:13:39,202
May Allah have them fall in another one again.

188
00:13:40,829 --> 00:13:45,938
And whenever they get into trouble, May Allah let them find anybody to take them out of that trouble.

189
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:50,396
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

190
00:13:51,016 --> 00:13:56,147
Paradise is for him, who holds the reins of his horse to strive in Allah’s cause

191
00:13:56,723 --> 00:14:00,321
with his hair unkempt and feet covered with dust.

192
00:14:01,187 --> 00:14:06,639
If he is appointed in the vanguard, he is perfectly satisfied with his post of guarding.

193
00:14:07,307 --> 00:14:11,772
If he is appointed to the rear ward, he accepts his post with satisfaction.

194
00:14:12,951 --> 00:14:18,501
He is so simple and unambiguous, that if he asks for permission, he is not permitted.

195
00:14:18,842 --> 00:14:21,947
And if he intercedes, his intercession is not accepted.

196
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:23,821
And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

197
00:14:24,304 --> 00:14:28,559
This is the personality of the Ideal Muslim soldier.

198
00:14:32,138 --> 00:14:39,399
He is living a life of difficulty, first of all, because he is a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

199
00:14:41,092 --> 00:14:44,461
he can't even find a barber to take care of his hair,

200
00:14:46,352 --> 00:14:50,646
his hair is unkempt his feet are loaded with dust.

201
00:14:50,933 --> 00:14:52,212
His clothes are simple.

202
00:14:53,515 --> 00:14:55,351
Nevertheless, he's still satisfied with that.

203
00:14:56,139 --> 00:14:58,780
And wherever the Ameer(أمير) would put him, he'll be happy.

204
00:14:59,415 --> 00:15:05,467
So the second quality that he has is Ta’aa(طاعة), obedience, put me in the rear, I'm very pleased.

205
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:07,811
You know, I'm not gonna just take it and swallow it.

206
00:15:08,196 --> 00:15:11,248
I'm happy! Put me in the front. I'm fine!

207
00:15:11,887 --> 00:15:15,023
Have me guard for the entire night, I will be happy with it.

208
00:15:16,722 --> 00:15:20,534
And then it's the life of commitment, he is on his horse Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

209
00:15:21,887 --> 00:15:23,253
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

210
00:15:23,869 --> 00:15:28,552
Paradise is for him, who holds the reins of his horse to strive in Allah’s cause.

211
00:15:29,163 --> 00:15:31,495
So he has dedicated his life to this cause.

212
00:15:32,265 --> 00:15:35,284
It's not a seasonal thing for him.

213
00:15:37,084 --> 00:15:43,363
And then add to that, you know, he's doing all of this to serve the Ummah(امة),

214
00:15:45,255 --> 00:15:56,511
but because he didn't get to establish a wide network of friendship and business relations and,

215
00:15:57,317 --> 00:15:58,943
you know he's not part of that game.

216
00:15:59,392 --> 00:16:00,131
Nobody knows him.

217
00:16:01,187 --> 00:16:05,381
He's a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), that's ambiguous nobody knows who he is.

218
00:16:06,285 --> 00:16:10,728
So if it goes to make Shafa'a(شفاعة) for someone over himself, he's turned down.

219
00:16:11,027 --> 00:16:15,659
If he seeks permission to come into a place, nobody allows him, because nobody knows him.

220
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:20,191
So in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), he is obscure.

221
00:16:21,369 --> 00:16:26,146
His name is not even known, but to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,  Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ knows him very well.

222
00:16:27,432 --> 00:16:33,654
And there are plenty of soldiers like this in the Ummah(امة), in every generation.

223
00:16:35,064 --> 00:16:40,146
And these were the ones, who did the brunt of the fighting.

224
00:16:41,434 --> 00:16:46,283
It is their blood that conveyed to us the Islam that we know

225
00:16:47,607 --> 00:16:49,335
and we don't even know who their names are.

226
00:16:49,543 --> 00:16:52,141
And that's why when we will read that,

227
00:16:52,675 --> 00:16:55,581
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) once was receiving news about one of the battles,

228
00:16:55,661 --> 00:16:58,695
so they were telling them about all of the people who died whom were known.

229
00:17:00,514 --> 00:17:03,882
But then they said then, other people that you do not know

230
00:17:03,969 --> 00:17:08,029
but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) interrupted and said but Allah knows them, Allah knows them very well.

231
00:17:11,565 --> 00:17:17,689
So they have humbleness, they are sincere, they are not doing it for fame.

232
00:17:18,659 --> 00:17:21,241
Abdullah bin Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو) narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

233
00:17:21,467 --> 00:17:23,681
Two eyes will not be touched by hellfire.

234
00:17:24,309 --> 00:17:30,602
An eye that cries from the fear of Allah, and an eye that spent the night in the guarding post, in the path of Allah,

235
00:17:31,622 --> 00:17:32,415
this is in At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ).

236
00:17:34,363 --> 00:17:35,712
Abu Rehanah(أبوريحانة) narrates:

237
00:17:36,519 --> 00:17:39,492
We were with the Messenger of Allah, in an expedition.

238
00:17:40,499 --> 00:17:45,878
During our travel, we passed over a high place, and we spent our night in that location.

239
00:17:46,759 --> 00:17:51,393
The weather was very cold so I saw some people digging for themselves holes in the ground.

240
00:17:52,097 --> 00:17:57,845
They will then crawling to them and cover themselves with their shields to protect themselves from the cold weather.

241
00:17:58,417 --> 00:18:03,283
So imagine, digging for yourself a hole in the ground and then you crawl into it, and hide.

242
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:06,594
First of all because the ground is a bit warmer it retains more of the heat.

243
00:18:07,112 --> 00:18:14,504
Plus it shields you from the wind, and Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would have a mantel one piece of cloth to wrap them

244
00:18:14,578 --> 00:18:16,088
but it wouldn't be sufficient.

245
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:18,424
And sometimes it could get quite cold in the desert,

246
00:18:19,590 --> 00:18:25,640
the temperatures, shoot up very fast during the daytime and they sink, very fast at night.

247
00:18:26,238 --> 00:18:27,403
So you have both extremes.

248
00:18:27,862 --> 00:18:29,989
So now they're hiding in those holes,

249
00:18:30,193 --> 00:18:32,940
and they're covering themselves with their shields

250
00:18:33,795 --> 00:18:37,520
and cover themselves with their shields to protect themselves from the cold weather.

251
00:18:37,860 --> 00:18:39,989
When the Messenger of Allah, saw that he said:

252
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:43,311
Who would be our guard tonight and I would pray for him.?

253
00:18:43,995 --> 00:18:50,500
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ offered this incentive because of the condition was quite cold.

254
00:18:51,258 --> 00:18:52,279
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

255
00:18:52,319 --> 00:18:54,744
I will pray for you if you if you come forward.

256
00:18:55,375 --> 00:18:58,360
So one of the Ansaar(أنصار) stepped forward and said: I would O Messenger of Allah!.

257
00:18:59,197 --> 00:19:03,492
So Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to come close to him and then he asked him, his name.

258
00:19:04,465 --> 00:19:07,835
After the man replied the Messenger of Allah made a long prayer for him.

259
00:19:09,040 --> 00:19:13,735
Abu Rehana(أبوريحانة) is saying when I heard the prayer of the messenger of Allah I went to him and said:

260
00:19:13,775 --> 00:19:15,007
I also want to be a guard.

261
00:19:16,893 --> 00:19:20,177
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him come close.

262
00:19:20,687 --> 00:19:22,715
And then he asked me who I was?

263
00:19:22,755 --> 00:19:24,455
I said: Abu Rehana(أبوريحانة).

264
00:19:24,839 --> 00:19:28,032
He then made a prayer for me and it was shorter than the earlier one.

265
00:19:30,206 --> 00:19:31,005
Then he said:

266
00:19:31,382 --> 00:19:35,177
Hellfire is prohibited from an eye that cries from the fear of Allah

267
00:19:35,574 --> 00:19:40,129
and hellfire is prohibited from an eye that was awake, guarding in the path of Allah,

268
00:19:41,018 --> 00:19:44,547
Ahmad(أحمد), Musannaf Ibn Shaibah(مصنف إبن شَيبة), and An-Nasai(ألنسائ) and Ibn Hakim(إبن حاكم).

269
00:19:47,276 --> 00:19:48,426
Madhool(مدخول) narrates,

270
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:54,811
whoever spends the night guarding in the path of Allah until the morning would have all of his sins fall away.

271
00:19:55,421 --> 00:19:57,027
Musannaf Ibn Abi Shaibah(مصنف إبن أبي شَيبة).

272
00:19:58,455 --> 00:20:01,216
Sahal Bin Hanzalia(سهل ابن الحنظلية) said:

273
00:20:01,296 --> 00:20:05,914
They were with the Messenger of Allah, on the day of Hunain(حنين), we walked that entire day.

274
00:20:06,538 --> 00:20:09,200
A night he came to the Messenger of Allah and said:

275
00:20:10,018 --> 00:20:13,992
O Messenger of Allah, I went ahead of you until I reached, so and so mountain,

276
00:20:14,425 --> 00:20:19,688
and I found all of their Hawazin(هوازن) with their woman, camels and sheep, assembling at Hunain(حنين).

277
00:20:20,876 --> 00:20:22,548
The Messenger of Allah, smiled and said:

278
00:20:22,812 --> 00:20:26,536
Those will be a booty for the Muslims tomorrow In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله).

279
00:20:27,953 --> 00:20:32,458
Possibly Rasool Allah ﷺ could have received a promise from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ that this would, this would happen.

280
00:20:34,210 --> 00:20:39,727
But the other possibility is that this was a reflection of the personality of Rasool Ullah.

281
00:20:42,853 --> 00:20:47,777
Whenever he would receive news that could be seen as demoralizing,

282
00:20:48,778 --> 00:20:55,672
Rasool Allah ﷺ would turn it around into good news to raise the morale of the army.

283
00:20:57,724 --> 00:21:01,242
So here, this man is coming to Rasool Allah ﷺ with a bad piece of news.

284
00:21:01,773 --> 00:21:04,667
Hunain(حنين) with their women, with their children.

285
00:21:04,911 --> 00:21:08,248
You know when they would have their women and children with them,

286
00:21:08,288 --> 00:21:11,527
that's an indication that they're taking the battle very seriously.

287
00:21:12,173 --> 00:21:15,104
Similar situation happened in Ghazwa Al-Khandaq(غزوة الخندق).

288
00:21:15,763 --> 00:21:21,834
And by the way, Ghazwa Al-Khandaq(غزوة الخندق) was one of the worst moments for the Muslims.

289
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:26,020
You had an army of 10,000 surrounding Madina.

290
00:21:26,808 --> 00:21:34,665
It was a coalition of various Arab tribes, alongside the Jews with Munafiqeen(مُنافقين) from within, assisting them.

291
00:21:36,381 --> 00:21:40,120
So, it was a very, very tough time for the Muslims.

292
00:21:41,937 --> 00:21:45,174
And that's, by the way when the Ayah(آية) was revealed.

293
00:21:45,803 --> 00:21:54,138
إِذ جاءوكُم مِن فَوقِكُم وَمِن أَسفَلَ مِنكُم

294
00:21:54,525 --> 00:22:04,364
وَإِذ زاغَتِ الأَبصارُ وَبَلَغَتِ القُلوبُ الحَناجِرَ وَتَظُنّونَ بِاللَّهِ الظُّنونا۞

295
00:22:05,060 --> 00:22:12,225
 هُنالِكَ ابتُلِيَ المُؤمِنونَ وَزُلزِلوا زِلزالًا شَديدًا۞

296
00:22:12,608 --> 00:22:21,132
They attacked you from above and from beneath and your hearts are pounding in your throats and your eyes are dizzy.

297
00:22:21,802 --> 00:22:27,876
إِذ جاءوكُم مِن فَوقِكُم وَمِن أَسفَلَ مِنكُم وَإِذ زاغَتِ الأَبصارُ وَبَلَغَتِ القُلوبُ الحَناجِرَ وَتَظُنّونَ بِاللَّهِ الظُّنونا۞

298
00:22:28,223 --> 00:22:29,233
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

299
00:22:29,974 --> 00:22:34,040
هُنالِكَ ابتُلِيَ المُؤمِنونَ وَزُلزِلوا زِلزالًا شَديدًا۞

300
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:36,373
It was a Zilzal(زلزال), Zilzal(زلزال) is an earthquake.

301
00:22:36,819 --> 00:22:38,458
It was an earthquake for the believers.

302
00:22:39,096 --> 00:22:42,290
So that was one of the toughest moments on the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

303
00:22:44,238 --> 00:22:49,189
the toughest moment of all within Al-Khandaq(ألخندق),

304
00:22:50,705 --> 00:22:58,135
was when the news was brought to Rasool Allah ﷺ that Banu Quraidha(بنوقريظة) have broken their agreement with the Rasool Allah ﷺ.

305
00:22:58,215 --> 00:23:00,400
This was, the catastrophe.

306
00:23:01,396 --> 00:23:03,656
Because Banu Quraidha(بنوقريظة) were within the city limits.

307
00:23:07,056 --> 00:23:12,573
Al-Madina(ألمدينة) was surrounded by some natural production, you had Al-Harrah Sharqiyah Wal Harrah Gharbiyyah(حرَّة شرقية والحرة غربية).

308
00:23:13,190 --> 00:23:15,527
These are rocky volcanic tracks.

309
00:23:16,273 --> 00:23:21,303
These are not mountains, it's level plan but it has a lot of volcanic rocks and they're very sharp.

310
00:23:22,765 --> 00:23:25,450
And it makes it very difficult for an army to march through it.

311
00:23:25,761 --> 00:23:28,575
So that was a natural protection from Madina from the east and the west,

312
00:23:29,607 --> 00:23:34,616
from the south, you had the palm groves, miles and miles of palm groves.

313
00:23:35,313 --> 00:23:40,060
So, the attack would come from the north.

314
00:23:40,495 --> 00:23:42,723
If Madina would be attacked, it will be attacked from the North.

315
00:23:43,273 --> 00:23:44,980
That's where the Sahabah(صحابه) dug the trench.

316
00:23:45,482 --> 00:23:49,941
But the problem is that now Banu Quraidha(بنوقريظة) are within the city limits and,

317
00:23:51,221 --> 00:23:54,452
Rasool Allah ﷺ had an agreement with them, a peace agreement,

318
00:23:55,105 --> 00:24:03,515
and the peak hour Banu Quraidha(بنوقريظة) break their agreement with Rasool Allah ﷺ, and join in hands with the coalition.

319
00:24:03,857 --> 00:24:07,851
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked one of the Sahabah(صحابه) to go and check if the news was true

320
00:24:07,891 --> 00:24:13,441
because Rasool Allah ﷺ heard a rumor that Banu Quraidha(بنوقريظة) have betrayed, they have committed treason.

321
00:24:14,123 --> 00:24:16,554
So Rasool Ullah sent two of the Sahabah(صحابه), he said:

322
00:24:16,792 --> 00:24:18,738
Go and investigate the matter for me.

323
00:24:19,625 --> 00:24:24,345
If you found that they are still up to their word, tell me publicly.

324
00:24:25,630 --> 00:24:28,907
If you find out that they have committed treason, give me a sign.

325
00:24:31,088 --> 00:24:36,835
So they went, they found out that Banu Quraidha(بنوقريظة) have betrayed their agreement so they came back to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

326
00:24:37,256 --> 00:24:44,361
and they gave him a sign, without speaking that Banu Quraidha(بنوقريظة) have actually betrayed the agreement.

327
00:24:44,422 --> 00:24:50,806
I think the call on the sign was I think like a slit of a throat or something, and Rasool Allah ﷺ have understood that.

328
00:24:51,368 --> 00:24:52,594
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ say?

329
00:24:53,611 --> 00:24:59,343
And look at the orders of Rasool Ullah, Don't make it publicly because he doesn't want to demoralize the Muslims.

330
00:25:00,369 --> 00:25:04,407
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Abshiru(أبشِرو)! Rejoice with the good news.

331
00:25:05,024 --> 00:25:05,988
He didn't tell him what it was.

332
00:25:06,068 --> 00:25:07,655
He said: Abshiru(أبشرو)! Be happy!

333
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:10,632
So he would turn everything around.

334
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:16,886
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) that positiveness was also inherited by the Khalifah(خليفه) after him,

335
00:25:17,300 --> 00:25:20,420
khalifa-Tu-Rasul Ullah(خليفةالرسول الله), Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

336
00:25:23,774 --> 00:25:29,451
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would receive these news about what's happening with the Murtaddeen(مرتدين),

337
00:25:30,040 --> 00:25:32,339
and it would only make Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) stronger and stronger,

338
00:25:33,320 --> 00:25:36,041
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was asked. He was told,

339
00:25:36,596 --> 00:25:42,241
لقد نزل بك ما لو نزل بالجبال لهاضها ولو نزل بالبحارلغاصها

340
00:25:44,305 --> 00:25:52,691
The disasters that befell you, if they fell on a mountain, the mountain would break.

341
00:25:52,803 --> 00:25:55,432
And if it fell on the oceans, the oceans would sink.

342
00:25:57,008 --> 00:25:58,440
How were you able to handle them.

343
00:25:59,689 --> 00:26:01,592
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

344
00:26:02,432 --> 00:26:05,618
Since I had fear with Rasool Allah ﷺ in the cave in Hijrah(هجرة).

345
00:26:06,167 --> 00:26:07,381
I never had fear after that.

346
00:26:09,479 --> 00:26:15,451
Why because that is when Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ revealed the Ayaat(آيات) that say,

347
00:26:15,913 --> 00:26:20,604
إِذ يَقولُ لِصاحِبِهِ لا تَحزَن إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَنا ۖ

348
00:26:21,352 --> 00:26:24,873
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is telling Muhammadﷺ, to tell your companion:

349
00:26:25,394 --> 00:26:29,824
Don't have sadness or sorrow because Allah is with you.

350
00:26:30,308 --> 00:26:31,720
He said: I never felt fear after that,

351
00:26:32,781 --> 00:26:37,971
when he sent out the four armies to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

352
00:26:39,201 --> 00:26:42,943
The army of Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح), the army of Yazeed Bin Abi Sufyaan(يزيدبن أبي سفيان),

353
00:26:43,390 --> 00:26:46,791
the army of Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة), and the army of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

354
00:26:46,979 --> 00:26:48,093
Four armies into Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

355
00:26:49,814 --> 00:26:51,737
The objective was to open Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

356
00:26:53,765 --> 00:26:57,429
And Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) was under the control of the Romans.

357
00:26:58,666 --> 00:27:03,795
The Romans took this advance quite seriously, so they assembled huge armies.

358
00:27:04,994 --> 00:27:09,554
These armies that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) sent were averaging about 4000 each.

359
00:27:10,260 --> 00:27:15,025
The Romans would meet them with 50,000, 70,000, 90,000 each.

360
00:27:16,295 --> 00:27:21,421
Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) sent in a letter to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, telling him.

361
00:27:22,946 --> 00:27:25,386
It's a long letter but two important points.

362
00:27:25,899 --> 00:27:26,362
He said:

363
00:27:26,452 --> 00:27:29,528
Heracul(هراقل) has moved from his capital Constantinople,

364
00:27:29,969 --> 00:27:33,331
and set base in Antakia(أنتاكية) in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) to be close to the events.

365
