745
00:54:59,122 --> 00:55:03,540
They should thank Allah for giving them health and strength to practice

746
00:55:03,985 --> 00:55:06,390
and should praise Allah for making it beloved to them.

747
00:55:07,122 --> 00:55:10,614
It is acceptable to laugh and play with your brother, while practicing

748
00:55:11,041 --> 00:55:16,031
in fact it is recommended since it makes target shooting dearer to you.

749
00:55:16,758 --> 00:55:17,893
Bilal Bin Saad(بلال بن سعد) said:

750
00:55:18,612 --> 00:55:23,132
I have seen men, who would run between their targets and joke with each other.

751
00:55:23,467 --> 00:55:25,929
But when night arrives they would turn into monks.

752
00:55:27,206 --> 00:55:28,291
Bilal(بلال) was one of them.

753
00:55:28,855 --> 00:55:32,493
He was one of the great scholars of At-Taba'een(ألتابعين) and one of their worshipers,

754
00:55:33,149 --> 00:55:36,456
he was among the ones, who would pray a 1000s Rak'ah(ركعة) per night.

755
00:55:38,260 --> 00:55:41,508
Shams-Ud-Din Al-Joziya(سمش الدين ألجوزية) stated in his book knighthood,

756
00:55:42,429 --> 00:55:43,589
that Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) said:

757
00:55:44,091 --> 00:55:49,805
It is narrated that some men were target shooting, when it was told to the Messenger of Allah, it's time for prayers,

758
00:55:50,193 --> 00:55:51,951
he said: They are in prayers.

759
00:55:52,702 --> 00:55:55,500
So he considered that their target shooting is equivalent to praying.

760
00:55:58,123 --> 00:56:01,297
If I can relate this to what I was saying yesterday,

761
00:56:01,720 --> 00:56:06,394
in some countries, you don't have access to ranges.

762
00:56:08,813 --> 00:56:15,054
So you need to look at it that if you are deprived from all of this Ajr(أجْر), you want to make it up, you must make it up.

763
00:56:17,003 --> 00:56:20,164
And the way, it could be, you could make it up as by the Jihad Bil Maal(جهاد بالمال),

764
00:56:21,121 --> 00:56:24,401
by exercising and doing other forms of recreation.

765
00:56:25,423 --> 00:56:29,838
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ rewards for the intention as long as a person is doing the best that they could.

766
00:56:31,668 --> 00:56:38,295
But the fact that the person cannot actually practice target shooting does not mean that that's it, you just give up.

767
00:56:39,477 --> 00:56:44,475
Do the best, and you push it to the limits of what is possible.

768
00:56:45,296 --> 00:56:49,573
And then you expect to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to give you the Ajr(أجْر), according to your Niyyah(نية).

769
00:56:52,753 --> 00:56:55,844
Rules of betting on racing and target shooting.

770
00:56:56,337 --> 00:57:05,045
Now, these rules, they seem complicated, or we can't really relate to them.

771
00:57:05,816 --> 00:57:14,454
Don't be worried about it, I just translated this to sole purpose of showing how the early Muslims gave attention to this,

772
00:57:14,940 --> 00:57:18,305
to the extent that they have all of these elaborate rules about it.

773
00:57:22,145 --> 00:57:23,091
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

774
00:57:23,196 --> 00:57:26,015
When I've seen that some who practice horseback racing,

775
00:57:26,421 --> 00:57:30,894
and target shooting are involved in financial dealings that are inappropriate for Shariah(شريعة) standpoint,

776
00:57:31,450 --> 00:57:35,585
I decided to write a brief chapter on the rules that govern racing and target shooting.

777
00:57:36,255 --> 00:57:39,966
The first of our scholars to write an entire book on the subject is Imam Shafie(إمام شافعي),

778
00:57:40,698 --> 00:57:44,429
and that's why people of our Madh'hab(مذهب) are the most elaborate on the topic.

779
00:57:45,099 --> 00:57:48,754
Then come the followers of  Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) since he was a student of Imam Shafie(إمام شافعي)

780
00:57:49,155 --> 00:57:50,584
and a follower of his Sunnah(سنة) in that

781
00:57:51,064 --> 00:57:57,860
I bridged it, the chapter is quite long, but this is a bridged version of it.

782
00:57:58,253 --> 00:57:58,852
RACING.

783
00:57:59,553 --> 00:58:01,583
It is the consensus of the scholars of the Ummah(امة)

784
00:58:02,006 --> 00:58:06,875
that competitions in horse racing and target shooting are not only allowed, but are Sunnah(سنة),

785
00:58:07,291 --> 00:58:15,483
and the one who participates in them would be rewarded as long as the intentions is to prepare for the Jihad(جهاد).

786
00:58:15,618 --> 00:58:19,381
Rules of betting on target race on horseback racing.

787
00:58:20,006 --> 00:58:26,318
Number one, race needs to involve an animal that could be used in Jihad(جهاد), such as a horse or a camel,

788
00:58:27,183 --> 00:58:33,418
as is the consensus of the scholars, and in mules, donkeys and elephants, according to our Madh'hab(مذهب).

789
00:58:33,883 --> 00:58:39,141
So these must be animals that are used for Jihad(جهاد),

790
00:58:39,191 --> 00:58:43,139
for example, you can't really have chicken racing or Beatles racing, or…

791
00:58:43,762 --> 00:58:45,977
it has to be an animal that could be used for Jihad(جهاد).

792
00:58:46,544 --> 00:58:50,275
And that's why there's a difference of opinion when it comes to mules, donkeys and elephants,

793
00:58:50,658 --> 00:58:54,960
because some say that Muslims don't use them in Jihad(جهاد).

794
00:58:55,198 --> 00:59:00,181
Number two, the existence of a clear starting and ending point.

795
00:59:00,928 --> 00:59:02,552
Otherwise, the race is invalid.

796
00:59:02,691 --> 00:59:06,954
Number three, the entire amount of money or at least most of it goes to the winner.

797
00:59:07,333 --> 00:59:11,059
Number four, If the two racers themselves contribute the money

798
00:59:11,377 --> 00:59:15,499
there needs to be a third person with them, this third person would get all the money if he wins,

799
00:59:15,791 --> 00:59:17,270
but if they win, he gives them nothing.

800
00:59:17,788 --> 00:59:22,340
The one who wins among the two would get the money contributed by both.

801
00:59:22,665 --> 00:59:26,974
Number five, there needs to be a feasibility that any one of the races could win,

802
00:59:27,531 --> 00:59:30,952
meaning it is not impossible for one of them to win due to disadvantage.

803
00:59:31,374 --> 00:59:35,948
Otherwise the race is considered unfair, and it becomes invalid from a Shariah(شريعة) point of view.

804
00:59:36,270 --> 00:59:43,739
Number six, the identification and agreement on the specific horses or camels participating prior to the race.

805
00:59:43,843 --> 00:59:48,016
Number seven, the identification and agreement on the riders prior to the race.

806
00:59:48,492 --> 00:59:51,903
Number eight, the distance of the race needs to be possible to finish.

807
00:59:51,986 --> 00:59:53,068
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) said:

808
00:59:53,463 --> 00:59:59,223
The Messenger of Allah had the horses trained for racing run from Hafiyah(حافية) to Saniah Tul Wida(ثنية الوداع).

809
01:00:00,422 --> 01:00:05,605
While he had the untrained horses raised from Saniah Tul Wida(ثنية الوداع) to the Masjid(مسجد) of Banu Zuraiq(بنوزريق).

810
01:00:06,683 --> 01:00:11,003
The training of horses for racing at that time involved, among other things,

811
01:00:11,471 --> 01:00:16,997
gradual reduction of their diet for them to become slimmer and more capable of running.

812
01:00:17,928 --> 01:00:23,359
Sufian(سفيان) said: The distance between Hafiyah(حافية) and Saniah Tul Wida(ثنية الوداع), is five to six miles

813
01:00:23,722 --> 01:00:27,108
and the distance between the Saniah Tul Wida(ثنية الوداع) and Masjid(مسجد) of Banu Zuraiq(بنوزريق) is one mile.

814
01:00:27,688 --> 01:00:30,207
Number nine, the agreement on the amount of the betting money.

815
01:00:30,495 --> 01:00:35,526
Number 10, The avoidance of conditions that invalidate the contract.

816
01:00:35,957 --> 01:00:40,361
The rules of betting on target shooting.

817
01:00:40,930 --> 01:00:45,517
Number one, the existence of a third person if both archers contribute the money.

818
01:00:45,584 --> 01:00:49,182
Number two, the similarity of the equipment used for example,

819
01:00:49,909 --> 01:00:54,695
it is not allowed for one party to use a bow and arrow while the other is using a spear.

820
01:00:55,167 --> 01:00:59,822
Number three, the target needs not to be impossible to strike nor too easy.

821
01:00:59,864 --> 01:01:01,152
But should it be possible to strike.

822
01:01:01,252 --> 01:01:05,620
Number four, all of the following needs to be specified before the competition,

823
01:01:05,661 --> 01:01:07,340
 the amount of money contributed to the betting.

824
01:01:07,783 --> 01:01:09,130
The number of shots to be fired,

825
01:01:09,476 --> 01:01:11,321
the distance in which to shoot from

826
01:01:11,684 --> 01:01:14,123
and the order in which the participants to shoot.

827
01:01:14,532 --> 01:01:18,824
Number five, the specifications of the two competitors prior to the competition.

828
01:01:19,125 --> 01:01:23,586
Number six, the starting position needs to be specified and it should be equal for both.

829
01:01:25,775 --> 01:01:29,488
The warning against whoever learns, shooting and then deserts it.

830
01:01:30,369 --> 01:01:32,334
Fakheem Al Lakhvi(فخيم ألَكْوي), told Uqbah Bin Amir(عقبة بن عامر),

831
01:01:33,080 --> 01:01:37,021
you are running between these two targets and you are at this old age.

832
01:01:37,368 --> 01:01:37,994
Uqbah(عقبة) said:

833
01:01:38,805 --> 01:01:43,920
If it wasn't for some words, I heard from the Messenger of Allah, I wouldn't have gone through this.

834
01:01:44,761 --> 01:01:47,502
The narrator asked what those words were, he said:

835
01:01:47,907 --> 01:01:52,768
Whoever learns target shooting and then abandons it, is not one of us,

836
01:01:53,405 --> 01:01:55,311
or he said: Has committed the sin.

837
01:01:55,633 --> 01:01:56,846
And this is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح ألمسلم).

838
01:01:56,924 --> 01:01:58,022
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

839
01:01:59,463 --> 01:02:04,483
Some of the scholars are of the opinion that learning target shooting and then abandoning it,

840
01:02:04,744 --> 01:02:06,102
is one of the major sins

841
01:02:06,684 --> 01:02:09,937
based on the rule that whenever the Messenger of Allah says:

842
01:02:10,346 --> 01:02:13,108
He is not one of us, or a statement similar to that,

843
01:02:13,513 --> 01:02:14,879
it is referring to a major sin,

844
01:02:15,267 --> 01:02:19,706
and the scholars says that whatever carries the threat of Hellfire in Qur'an,

845
01:02:20,136 --> 01:02:23,514
or whenever Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث) that he doesn't belong to us.

846
01:02:24,035 --> 01:02:25,326
That is a major sin.

847
01:02:26,618 --> 01:02:27,971
The virtues of swords,

848
01:02:28,514 --> 01:02:29,204
Allah says:

849
01:02:29,538 --> 01:02:38,656
فَإِذا قَضَيتُمُ الصَّلاةَ فَاذكُرُوا اللَّهَ قِيامًا وَقُعودًا وَعَلىٰ جُنوبِكُم ۚ

850
01:02:39,095 --> 01:02:50,886
فَإِذَا اطمَأنَنتُم فَأَقيمُوا الصَّلاةَ ۚ إِنَّ الصَّلاةَ كانَت عَلَى المُؤمِنينَ كِتابًا مَوقوتًا۞

851
01:02:51,136 --> 01:02:55,462
And let them carry their arms and that’s in An-Nisa(ألنساء) verse 103.

852
01:02:55,955 --> 01:02:56,494
Allah says:

853
01:02:57,124 --> 01:03:10,338
وَأَعِدّوا لَهُم مَا استَطَعتُم مِن قُوَّةٍ وَمِن رِباطِ الخَيلِ تُرهِبونَ بِهِ عَدُوَّ اللَّهِ وَعَدُوَّكُم

854
01:03:11,148 --> 01:03:19,532
وَعَدُوَّكُم وَآخَرينَ مِن دونِهِم لا تَعلَمونَهُمُ اللَّهُ يَعلَمُهُم ۚ

855
01:03:20,050 --> 01:03:31,283
وَما تُنفِقوا مِن شَيءٍ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ يُوَفَّ إِلَيكُم وَأَنتُم لا تُظلَمونَ۞

856
01:03:31,350 --> 01:03:33,675
And prepare against them, whatever you are able to power.

857
01:03:33,710 --> 01:03:34,633
Al-Anfal(ألأنفال) Verse 60.

858
01:03:36,158 --> 01:03:37,687
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

859
01:03:38,222 --> 01:03:43,856
I was sent right before the final hour with the sword, until Allah is worshipped with no associates.

860
01:03:44,411 --> 01:03:46,517
بعثت بين يدي الساعة بالسيف،

861
01:03:48,263 --> 01:03:50,915
 And my provisions are under the shade of my spear,

862
01:03:50,995 --> 01:03:53,311
وجعل رزقي تحت ظل رمحي

863
01:03:53,979 --> 01:03:58,052
And humility is the destiny of whoever goes against me.

864
01:03:58,408 --> 01:04:00,417
And whoever imitates the people, is one of them.

865
01:04:00,484 --> 01:04:02,443
And this is in the Musnad Imam Ahmad(مسنداِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ),

866
01:04:02,539 --> 01:04:05,976
Rasool Allah ﷺ is a comprehensive personality.

867
01:04:06,456 --> 01:04:13,141
So what happens is that Islamic ideology that are not comprehensive

868
01:04:13,488 --> 01:04:16,160
tend to look at Rasool Allah ﷺ from a specific angle,

869
01:04:16,987 --> 01:04:18,706
and they block out everything else.

870
01:04:20,983 --> 01:04:27,005
And you could find in Rasool Allah ﷺ different aspects to his personality, but they all complement each other.

871
01:04:27,552 --> 01:04:33,269
You would find some times stressing on the point that Rasool Allah ﷺ came to bring peace

872
01:04:34,362 --> 01:04:39,517
and that he was a peaceful man and that Islam is religion of peace.

873
01:04:40,929 --> 01:04:44,044
But Rasool Allah ﷺ also there's another side to his personality,

874
01:04:44,608 --> 01:04:49,147
and that is that he was carrying his sword Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), until he died.

875
01:04:50,096 --> 01:04:51,998
بعثت بالسيف بين يدي الساعة

876
01:04:52,131 --> 01:04:53,309
And Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying:

877
01:04:53,969 --> 01:04:56,871
He didn't say I was sent with the olive of branch.

878
01:04:57,614 --> 01:04:58,992
He said: I was sent with sword.

879
01:05:00,220 --> 01:05:02,580
This tells you something about the personality of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

880
01:05:02,647 --> 01:05:03,695
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

881
01:05:03,900 --> 01:05:05,383
وجعل رزقي تحت ظل رمحي

882
01:05:06,398 --> 01:05:09,281
We always say that Rasool Allah ﷺ was a shepherd and then he was a businessman.

883
01:05:09,582 --> 01:05:16,084
That was in Makkah, but later on his Rizq(رزق) was totally from Ghanaem(غنائم).

884
01:05:17,148 --> 01:05:20,040
And this is the greatest avenue of Rizq(رزق) and it is the most Halal(حلال).

885
01:05:21,118 --> 01:05:22,926
Because it was the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

886
01:05:23,256 --> 01:05:24,722
وجعل رزقي تحت ظل رمحي

887
01:05:25,156 --> 01:05:28,905
My Rizq(رزق) comes from beneath my spear that's how I make a living.

888
01:05:30,092 --> 01:05:34,072
While you find that other forms of Rizq(رزق), for example what is mentioned in the Hadith(حديث).

889
01:05:34,849 --> 01:05:38,551
إذا تبايعتم بالعِينةِ وأخذتم أذنابَ البقرِ ورضيتم بالزرعِ

890
01:05:38,965 --> 01:05:40,836
These are other forms of Rizq(رزق), that are Halal(حلال).

891
01:05:41,492 --> 01:05:43,659
Unless one would follow the opinion that Eena(عينة) is not,

892
01:05:43,948 --> 01:05:48,092
but the other two are, following the tails of cows and you're shepherd.

893
01:05:49,050 --> 01:05:51,977
وشغلتم  بالزرعِ

894
01:05:52,017 --> 01:05:54,661
You're busy with agriculture, agriculture is also Halal(حلال).

895
01:05:56,286 --> 01:05:58,919
But in this Hadith(حديث) it is looked down upon.

896
01:06:01,693 --> 01:06:06,808
If the ones in those professions have left Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

897
01:06:07,944 --> 01:06:12,472
So with the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم they weren't involved in any of the skilled work.

898
01:06:12,531 --> 01:06:17,000
They weren't involved in any of the professions, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were leading the nations of world.

899
01:06:17,840 --> 01:06:19,340
And their Rizq(رزق) would comes to Ghanaem(غنائم).

900
01:06:21,127 --> 01:06:29,127
When it came to the other types of work like agriculture and pottery and paving the roads and whatever,

901
01:06:29,776 --> 01:06:31,640
this wasn't something that Sahabah(صحابه) would do.

902
01:06:32,125 --> 01:06:34,777
The Sahabah(صحابه) would fight in the battlefield and live off their swords.

903
01:06:35,679 --> 01:06:37,362
That was the way of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

904
01:06:37,650 --> 01:06:40,872
They were not engineers or professors or doctors.

905
01:06:41,608 --> 01:06:44,992
I am not saying anything against these professions, but we're talking about what the Sahabah(صحابه) were.

906
01:06:46,261 --> 01:06:48,203
That was the way of the Sahabah(صحابه).

907
01:06:48,938 --> 01:06:54,163
The best way to summarize the personality of Rasool Allah ﷺ is through his own words.

908
01:06:54,714 --> 01:06:54,961
He said:

909
01:06:55,008 --> 01:06:57,717
أنا نبي الرَّحمة، أنَا نَبِيُّ المَلْحَمة

910
01:06:58,771 --> 01:07:01,710
I am the prophet of mercy, I am the prophet of war.

911
01:07:02,988 --> 01:07:03,581
And he said:

912
01:07:05,076 --> 01:07:06,278
أنِا ضحوك قتال

913
01:07:07,561 --> 01:07:10,874
I am the smiling Prophet, but I'm also the one, who kills.

914
01:07:12,214 --> 01:07:17,689
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ had that pleasant personality, soft personality, mercy, but his sword was very sharp.

915
01:07:18,654 --> 01:07:21,543
Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبنِ ألقَيِّم) said: Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) stated

916
01:07:22,067 --> 01:07:28,045
that training with your spear in places where Jihad(جهاد) is needed is greater and reward than voluntary Salah(صلاة).

917
01:07:28,950 --> 01:07:30,918
Put the right thing in the right place.

918
01:07:31,609 --> 01:07:37,530
You know when Napoleon rolled into Egypt, some of the Shyookh(شيوخ) of the Turk,

919
01:07:38,733 --> 01:07:41,130
they went into the Masjid(مسجد) and they started reading Bukhari(بخاريْ).

920
01:07:41,908 --> 01:07:43,797
They said: Bukhari(بخاريْ) will save us from Napoleon,

921
01:07:44,813 --> 01:07:49,855
reading Bukhari(بخاريْ) has his place and picking up your sword and going to fight has its place.

922
01:07:50,859 --> 01:07:53,192
Put the right thing the right place, that is Hikmah(حكمة).

923
01:07:53,653 --> 01:07:57,529
Hikmah(حكمة) is to do the right thing, the Right Place the right time, the right way.

924
01:07:57,759 --> 01:08:00,979
Abdullah Ibn Abi Aofa(عبدالله إبن أبي ‘وفة ) narrated

925
01:08:01,019 --> 01:08:05,164
that the Messenger of Allah was waiting for an enemy to attack but when the sun was setting, he said:

926
01:08:05,624 --> 01:08:07,229
Don't desire meeting the enemy,

927
01:08:07,775 --> 01:08:13,779
but when you do be firm, and realize that Paradise is beneath the shadow of the swords.

928
01:08:14,833 --> 01:08:21,279
The Muslim is not trigger happy seeking fighting, love chaos. No!

929
01:08:21,636 --> 01:08:22,843
لا تتمنو لِقَا ألعدو

930
01:08:23,175 --> 01:08:27,638
Don't ask for it. Don't ask for trouble. But when it comes you need to be fair.

931
01:08:28,376 --> 01:08:31,495
Abu Bakr Bin Musa(ابوبكر بن أبي موسى) said: I heard my father say,

932
01:08:31,583 --> 01:08:33,649
Paradise is beneath the shadow of swords.!

933
